ndings were not applied.","timestamp":1785206256298381001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Story 1934 final plan review PASS signed at 5f9f22673; DET P1-P9 all pass, 15 ACs, no blocking findings. One E1 advisory suggested asserting private _REGISTRY absence. Skipped with rationale: rebar-implement/test-design requires observable behavior rather than internal structure; the plan now explicitly verifies old JSON-array write state/stdout/exit code plus new --none behavior, which exercises the dispatch contract without coupling tests to registry internals.","timestamp":1785206956487076001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Epic plan review BLOCK on deterministic P1 only: existing checklist was headed Success Criteria rather than exact Acceptance Criteria. Renamed the heading without changing criterion content. Re-running the mandatory epic claim review; advisory findings remain to triage after a signable pass.","timestamp":1785207804842669001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Epic PASS advisory remediation applied before claim: S2 fingerprint basis remains legacy-compatible for undeclared/paths and adds a none-only marker, with legacy-manifest AC; S3 explicitly owns passing all_none into S2 classifier; S4 specifies applies-based trigger and structured sub-answer vocabulary; added S3 depends_on S4 to serialize orchestrator.py; parent S5 now correctly declares doc paths, plus reason rejection/persistence/judgment ACs. T11 missing-line advisory was already covered by S2 legacy-manifest tests. Epic signature intentionally stale after these material edits; refreshing now.","timestamp":1785208646465848001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Epic follow-up PASS advisories 